{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_83","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' ISSUE_COMMENTS.md && sed -n '1,260p' PR_COMMENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"Created MONDO:7770736 for TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy. Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n## Summary\n\nAdded new term MONDO:7770736, `TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy`, under `neurodevelopmental disorder`.\n\n## Rationale\n\nThe issue requested a new TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder term with MONDO:0700092 as the parent. I confirmed that MONDO already has `pontocerebellar hypoplasia type 2B` for TSEN2-related PCH, but the requested term captures a broader TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder concept with possible thrombotic microangiopathy/renal involvement.\n\nThe new term follows the disease-series-by-gene pattern:\n\n- `is_a: MONDO:0700092`\n- logical definition using `has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in` TSEN2\n- asserted TSEN2 relationship using verified HGNC:28422\n- term tracker item for issue #9956\n\nI also added `TRACK syndrome` as a narrow synonym based on PMID:34964109, which directly describes TSEN2-related atypical hemolytic uremic syndrome, craniofacial malformations, and kidney failure.\n\n## Checks Completed\n\n- Read issue title/body/comments from `__issue_context__.json`.\n- Attempted `aurelian fulltext` for all PMIDs from the issue; `aurelian` is not installed in this environment.\n- Reviewed PubMed/NCBI records for the issue PMIDs and PMID:34964109.\n- Verified TSEN2 as HGNC:28422 using the HGNC REST API.\n- Checked existing MONDO stanzas for the requested parent, existing TSEN2/PCH terms, and thrombotic microangiopathy.\n- Checked for MONDO:777 ID clashes and selected unused MONDO:7770736.\n- Added the term via the `terms/` checkin workflow.\n- Attempted the required `sh run.sh make NORM && mv NORM mondo-edit.obo`; this failed because `docker` is not installed.\n- Ran the same normalization target locally with available `owltools`/`robot`: `make NORM && mv NORM mondo-edit.obo`.\n- Ran syntax validation: `robot convert --catalog src/ontology/catalog-v001.xml -i src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo -f obo -o /tmp/mondo-edit.TMP.obo`.\n- Ran `git diff --check`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
